A //plumb directive on a blank method is rejected in discover. A blank method is
absent from its type’s method set, so without this guard it would later panic
during instantiation rather than emit code.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrBlankProvider
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type R struct{}

//plumb:build
func (r *R) _() int { return 0 }
